{"text": "This lens weighs more than a kilogram, and it costs more than the phone lying next to it. It's as long as your forearm, and it's packed with thick glass, because that's what the laws of optics demand if you want to zoom. Your phone is expected to do the same job, from a body less than nine millimetres thick, with a sensor about the size of your fingernail. By the rules that built that lens, this shouldn't work. It shouldn't zoom. It shouldn't hold steady in your hand. And at night, it should give you this. A dark, grainy mess. And yet, you get this. Handheld. No flash. So, how? To find out, we're going to follow a single ray of light, all the way through. Into a block of glass that folds it around four corners. Onto a chip of silicon that floats on magnets. Down into wells a thousandth of a millimetre wide. And then, into the part almost nobody talks about. Because the photo you end up with was never really taken. It was calculated.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "i", "s", " ", "l", "e", "n", "s", " ", "w", "e", "i", "g", "h", "s", " ", "m", "o", "r", "e", " ", "t", "h", "a", "n", " ", "a", " ", "k", "i", "l", "o", "g", "r", "a", "m", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "i", "t", " ", "c", "o", "s", "t", "s", " ", "m", "o", "r", "e", " ", "t", "h", "a", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "h", "o", "n", "e", " ", "l", "y", "i", "n", "g", " ", "n", "e", "x", "t", " ", "t", "o", " ", "i", "t", ".", " ", "I", "t", "'", "s", " ", "a", "s", " ", "l", "o", "n", "g", " ", "a", "s", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "f", "o", "r", "e", "a", "r", "m", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "i", "t", "'", "s", " ", "p", "a", "c", "k", "e", "d", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "t", "h", "i", "c", "k", " ", "g", "l", "a", "s", "s", ",", " ", "b", "e", "c", "a", "u", "s", "e", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", "'", "s", " ", "w", "h", "a", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "l", "a", "w", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "o", "p", "t", "i", "c", "s", " ", "d", "e", "m", "a", "n", "d", " ", "i", "f", " 